  "section_notes": "S1 is fully safe: all-incident reporting within 24 hours, customer notice within 72 hours, and no phase-in. S2 keeps 55 °C testing and a 5% threshold but does not automatically stop sales above it and allows open-ended corrective action, weakening the section and favoring Northwind. S3 uses a 12-month new-unit deadline and a 72-month retrofit deadline, which is acceptable but leans toward Northwind; S4 requires built-in suppression from 36 months, acceptable. S5 has an 8/100k notification trigger but leaves recall to regulator discretion, weakening the section and favoring Halcyon."
